# Release Delivery Procedure

Status: DONE
Milestone: M0 Procedure definition only
Dependencies: None
Execution status: NOT_STARTED

## Purpose

Deliver an immutable qualified artifact with accurate support, data, and maintenance guidance.

## Inputs

Candidate source/runtime/dependency identity; approved license/distribution choices;
packaging recipe; clean-machine results; owner UX approval; required capture evidence.

## Procedure

1. Build/freeze the candidate via root workstream 14 and audit its contents for private data.
2. Qualify its exact hash via workstream 13; rebuilding requires affected qualification again.
3. Finish the user/support guide via workstream15 and workflow06's source-matched handbook,
   synthetic images, public journal and HTML/PDF manifest. Resolve every required release blocker.
4. Obtain explicit publishing authorization and verify the intended destination/account permissions.
5. Sign only with an approved identity/key workflow where required; record actual warnings and limits.
6. Deliver immutable versioned artifacts/hashes/notices; do not overwrite historical evidence.
7. Confirm the delivered identity and clean first-run/recovery behavior.
8. Complete workstream 17 and final ledger/offload with actual local/published status and maintenance owner.

## Stop conditions

Required capture failure, artifact mismatch, data-loss/recovery defect, missing license/signing
or publication permission, unsupported runtime/OS, or missing owner usability acceptance.
Lack of publishing access is not authorization to change accounts or bypass restrictions.

## Tasks

- [x] Define candidate-before-qualification order, release gates, publication approval, and handoff.
- [x] Separate signing from reputation and a local package from public delivery.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The procedure produces an exact scoped delivery receipt rather than an inferred successful release.
- [x] Rollback/data-migration and requalification ownership are included in handoff.

